// Every ability word shares one body: the italicized label wraps whatever
// ability follows it [CR#207.2c]. `params`/`body` are hardcoded here rather
// than left as per-file params: every declaration takes exactly one
// `Ability` argument and wraps it the same way, so there is nothing for a
// file to override. `Quote(Param(0))` defers that hole past this
// meta-expansion to the produced declaration's own frame, where a real
// invocation resolves it against its own positional argument.
//
// `kinds` names the family first and the SEMANTIC kind second: the family
// (`AbilityWord`) is the declaration's identity, which
// `deckmaste_construction_core::macro_def::normalized_kind` reads, and
// `Ability` is the position this body occupies, which is what makes
// `Threshold(<ability>)` resolve where a card writes an ability. Both are
// registered kinds in `deckmaste_semantics_v2::ron::kinds`, so the produced
// declaration registers under each.
(
    name: "AbilityWord",
    kinds: [Macro],
    params: {
        "name": String,
        "spelling": String,
        "grammar": Elidable(Any),
    },
    body: (
        name: Param(name),
        kinds: [AbilityWord, Ability],
        params: [Ability],
        metadata: (
            spelling: Param(spelling),
            grammar: Param(grammar),
        ),
        body: ItalicHead(word: AbilityWord(label: Param(name)), ability: Quote(Param(0))),
    ),
)
